Alyssa (Docs): Heads-up: PR #4123 adds embed sharding examples for lyra-embed-8b but I found a broken link in the model card. Anyone free to review?

Mike (ML): I saw it — the card links to /docs/embeds/sharding which is 404 now. I can update the URL to the new guide under /guides/embeddings/sharding.

Sophia (SDK): Also noticed the SDK snippet still shows the old .embed(...) call. We should use the new embeddings API; example: 
```js
// node SDK example
const res = await client.embeddings.create({
  model: 'lyra-embed-8b',
  input: ['short text', 'another text']
});
```
I'll push a tiny fix.

Alyssa (Docs): Thanks @Sophia — can you also include a short client-side sharding example and mention runtime behavior? The runtime accepts X-Embed-Shard for internal tests but we shouldn't recommend it for public usage.

Samir (Eng): We don't want customers relying on X-Embed-Shard in hosted. Better to show deterministic slicing + hashing. Quick Node example I dropped in PR: 
```js
// simple shard by hashing example
function shardInputs(inputs, shardCount) {
  const shards = Array.from({length: shardCount}, () => []);
  inputs.forEach((txt, i) => {
    const bucket = hash(txt) % shardCount;
    shards[bucket].push(txt);
  });
  return shards;
}
// upload each shard as a separate embeddings.create call
```
Use pseudocode hash() or a stable library.

DocsBot: PR #4123 CI: embed smoke tests failing when single input > 8192 tokens for lyra-embed-8b quantized variant. @Mike can you confirm behavior and recommended note?

Mike (ML): Confirmed. The quantized-8bit variant will best-effort truncate sequences beyond 8192 and sometimes drop tail context; we should add an explicit limit note in the model card: "sequence_limit: 8192 (quantized-8bit: best-effort truncation)" and call out potential embedding quality degradation near the cutoff.

Eva (PM): Also can we add a one-liner about throughput vs latency when sharding? Product teams often miss the tradeoff.

Sophia (SDK): Added suggestion: "Tip: batch shards to improve throughput; keep per-shard payloads under ~400KB to avoid client-side timeouts." I'll include that in the snippet comments.

Alyssa (Docs): Nice. One last ask: the model-catalog index currently links /models/lyra -> the old slug. Can infra put a redirect to /catalog/models/lyra-embed-8b so links don't 404? @Samir

Samir (Eng): Filed infra-redirects#27 to add the redirect and update canonical slug. ETA ~30m; once live I will comment here.

Alyssa (Docs): :thumbsup: I'll wait for the redirect then merge PR #4123. Thanks everyone for the quick turnaround!

Samir (Eng): redirect deployed, tested the 301. Go ahead and merge after CI green.

Alyssa (Docs): Merged and backfilled the link in the catalog index. Closing the thread. :tada:
